From a6bceff4c3019db2d5c115631f4b0cf0581cc671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xs1128 <hipac1@lsalab.cs.nthu.edu.tw>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 18:18:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] RHS: difference all directions' fluxes in one pass on the
 fused HLLC path

On the in-kernel-reconstructing HLLC path (recon_riemann_fused) with the u-interface source fused into the flux
differences (adv_src_fused), each sweep direction now writes its own slab of flux_rsx_vf / flux_src_rsx_vf
(flux_per_dir), so flux_n(d) and flux_src_n(d) no longer share direction 1's arrays. The x, y and z
flux-difference kernels, each a read-modify-write of all of rhs, become one kernel after the last sweep
(s_add_flux_differences) that adds, per cell and equation, the same terms in the same order (x flux, x alpha*div(u),
y flux, y alpha*div(u), z ...) and stores rhs once. CBC still edits each direction's fluxes right after its sweep.

- m_riemann_state: flux_per_dir. HLLC's fused emission writes through FLX()/FSRC() accessors at the direction's
  component offset (foff, fsoff); the other emissions are unchanged.
- m_rhs: sizes the flux buffers by num_dims, points flux_n(d)/flux_src_n(d) at slab d, skips the per-direction
  Cartesian difference kernels, and calls s_add_flux_differences after the last direction.
- Costs (num_dims - 1) more flux buffers: about 1.3 GB at 201^3 per GPU.

perf3d 201^3, 1 H200, same node (669254, hgpn003): 37.72 -> 36.83 ms/step (-2.4 %), bitwise vs v5.7.0.
